T|dotnet build FKNRTD.CLI.sln -c Release -nodeReuse:false => 0 warnings, 0 errors
T|dotnet run --project tests/FKNRTD.SelfTest -c Release --no-build => 138/138
T|Piped, -no-color and NO_COLOR frames compared byte for byte at 60, 80, 100, 140 and 200 columns
B|LINE ENDINGS DIFFER BETWEEN COLOUR MODES. Stripping the escapes from a coloured frame does NOT leave exactly the colourless frame: the coloured output carries 0 carriage returns and the -no-color output carries 2. Identical at 60 and 80 columns, divergent at 100, 140 and 200 - that is, wherever the layout becomes two rows. The invariant is character-for-character equality, so the row separator must be the same sequence in both modes. The self-test that claims to cover this passed at 138/138, so it is testing the renderer's return value rather than what the command writes; it needs to cover the command's actual output.
B|AGENTS.md LINE 84 STILL UNAMENDED. It reads 'redirected output must emit no ANSI escapes', which the statusline now deliberately contradicts. This was an explicit acceptance criterion. A documented rule that contradicts the code is worse than one that is missing, and this file is the first thing another seat reads.
Q|Round 3 also carries a layout change to match a reference the user supplied, so these two findings travel with it rather than in a round of their own.
